<!--
  Synthetic World-Check-shaped fixture. Every name, identifier, narrative and place here is
  INVENTED (CLAUDE.md section 3: never copy a real listed name into a fixture).

  The SHAPE, unlike the previous version of this file, is not invented. It was rebuilt on
  2026-09-25 from scripts/New-FeedPathInventory.ps1 run against the real feed, which reports
  element paths, attribute names and coverage counts and never values. The shape the earlier
  fixture guessed at was two levels too shallow — person/first_name where the feed has
  person/names/first_name — and because nothing loaded this file through WorldCheckAdapter, the
  guess went unchallenged until the first real load rejected 99.83% of the feed (D12 B-6).

  Structural facts this file reproduces, each of which the inventory confirmed:
    * names nest under person/names, with aliases under person/names/aliases/alias
    * alternative_spelling packs several spellings into one element, semicolon-separated
    * age data nests under person/agedata, and dob is ONE value using 00 for unknown components
    * countries, passports, locations, keywords and narrative all nest under details
    * location carries its data in @city/@country/@state and is itself xsi:nil
    * passport carries an issuing @country
    * xsi:nil="true" is an asserted absence, distinct from an empty element

  Category codes are the real vocabulary the inventory observed (POLITICAL INDIVIDUAL, VESSEL,
  COUNTRY, ...); the four E-categories not seen in the head of the file (AIRCRAFT, WEBSITE, PORT,
  ADDRESS) are exercised here on the inference recorded in WorldCheckAdapter.E_CATEGORY_TYPES.
-->
